# `buri version` prints the toolchain's version, and inside a repository it
# prints exactly that — one line, and nothing about the repository.
#
# That "nothing" is the claim. `REPO.buri` used to pin a toolchain and this
# command used to report the pin, so the case that pinned the refusal is now
# the case that pins its absence: standing in a repository changes nothing
# about what `version` prints, because it no longer opens one.
#
# The recorded output names a version, so it moves when the toolchain's version
# moves. That is deliberate and it is not a maintenance cost: the diff is the
# release.
#
# `--verbose` adds the hash of the running executable, which no golden can hold
# — it is whichever `buri` the suite just compiled. `language/conformance.rs`'s
# `version_works_outside_a_repository` asserts that line instead, along with
# the clause that cannot be a repository case at all, since a case *is* a
# repository.
#
# Schema: the repository-case manifest, cli/tests/harness/case.rs. Textproto,
# but not a Buri file: only repo/ below is a Buri repository.

doc: "version prints the toolchain version and, inside a repository, nothing else"

run {
  args: ["version"]
  exit: 0
  golden: "version.txt"
}
